      ],
      "content": "LITTLE GADDESDEN       \tLITTLE GADDESDEN SP 91 SE \t\t\t\t\t(East side)                                        1/199                                   \tKinghams Meadow - -                                      \t\tII House. 1858 (on plaque) for Lord Brownlow as house for Head Clerk at Ashridge. Red brick with sandy red brick dressings and relieving arches to stone mullioned windows. Steep red tile roofs. A 1½ storeys, L-shaped house facing W with prominent gabled lucarne windows to upper floor. Assymmetrical design with gable at LH of W front with tall stair windows, porch to right with 'B' plaque over. Open timber porch on brick sills to arched entrance door. Tall octagonal chimney shafts with stone bases. Bracketed verges to gables. Listing NGR: SP9982612758"
    }
  ],
